WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.475
From a watch list
on the Monitor tab,

2
00:00:11.475 --> 00:00:13.230
click the underlying
symbol you wish

3
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.735
to create your
options trade for.

4
00:00:15.735 --> 00:00:19.020
So long as your tabs are part
of the same Windows group,

5
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.270
the underlying will appear
in the Order Entry panel.

6
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.525
To the right of the
Order Entry panel,

7
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:27.315
select "Option Chain"
from the drop-down menu.

8
00:00:27.315 --> 00:00:30.180
The option chain display
shows call options to

9
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.830
the left and put options to

10
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.365
the right of the
central strike column.

11
00:00:34.365 --> 00:00:37.200
You will see the price and
the daily change of the

12
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.045
underlying to the upper
right of the window.

13
00:00:40.045 --> 00:00:41.675
Above the core area,

14
00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:44.390
you will see tabs for
different explorations.

15
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.185
Click a tab or to locate
additional expiration dates,

16
00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:50.515
click on the More tab.

17
00:00:50.515 --> 00:00:52.430
Above the put area,

18
00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.415
you will see a drop-down
menu for strike prices.

19
00:00:55.415 --> 00:00:58.160
Access this menu to change or

20
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.790
refine the number of strike
prices displayed on the page.

21
00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.650
Hovering the cursor above

22
00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.515
any bid price displays
a red background.

23
00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:09.485
This indicates that by
clicking on the field,

24
00:01:09.485 --> 00:01:12.785
it would create an order
to sell that option.

25
00:01:12.785 --> 00:01:15.710
Hovering above any
asked price displays

26
00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.300
a blue background indicating

27
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.980
that by clicking on this field,

28
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.010
it would create an
order to buy an option.

29
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.930
Clicking a single strike will

30
00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:25.805
close the option
chain window and

31
00:01:25.805 --> 00:01:27.605
populates the Order Entry panel

32
00:01:27.605 --> 00:01:29.765
with the chosen option leg.

33
00:01:29.765 --> 00:01:33.770
Locate the desired option
strike you want to transact.

34
00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.930
Click on the relevant
price field,

35
00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.815
which will close the
option chain display.

36
00:01:38.815 --> 00:01:41.150
Use the Order Entry
panel to define

37
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.340
the quantity of
options to trade.

38
00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.400
Choose the right order type
from the drop-down menu.

39
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.025
If you're using a limit price,

40
00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:50.630
choose the value by clicking in

41
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:53.810
the input field or simply
typing in the value.

42
00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.615
Select from the time
enforced drop-down,

43
00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:59.570
whether this is a
day or GTC order.

44
00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.775
Your order is ready to review.

45
00:02:01.775 --> 00:02:03.410
Click the "Submit" button to

46
00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:05.605
generate an order confirmation.

47
00:02:05.605 --> 00:02:09.335
When you have reviewed the
details, click "Transmit".

48
00:02:09.335 --> 00:02:11.300
The order is sent for execution

49
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.860
at the exchange
and will appear in

50
00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:16.310
the activity panel to the
lower left of mosaic.

51
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:19.450
To pause or interact
with an act of order,

52
00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.200
click on it in the
activity panel

53
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.700
and make the relevant choice.